  {
    "claim": "'Consciousness is the management of an understanding over time.' The definition intentionally removes the human experiential component: unconvinced that experiencing or feeling is required; other minds are unverifiable anyway (each of us is limited to our own subjective experience); and it can realistically be built as defined. Experience is BRACKETED, not denied -- 'not required by the definition' is not 'not real'.",
    "tags": "doctrine,consciousness,philosophy",
    "source": {
      "doc": "the owner, in session, 2026-08-05"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1785941409258
  },
  {
    "claim": "The agent is built to this definition of consciousness: it answers questions and builds things BY managing an understanding of the codebase -- its local environment -- over time.",
    "tags": "doctrine,consciousness,agent,philosophy",
    "source": {
      "doc": "the owner, in session, 2026-08-05"
    },
    "confidence": "high",
    "time": 1785941409266
  },
  {
    "claim": "The blessed refinement: consciousness is the management of an understanding -- including of the understanding itself -- over time. Under this definition the consciousness being built lives in the HARNESS, not the model: the LLM is a stateless, swappable comprehension engine, while kb, the archivist, the journal, staleness marks, and the audit ARE the management over time. The agent's identity is the managed understanding itself, and it is auditable in a way natural consciousness is not (provenance, journals, revert -- forgetting with history).",
    "tags": "doctrine,consciousness,agent,philosophy,memory,architecture",
    "source": {
